description:
IT Infrastructure Management:
Ensure the network infrastructure (LAN, WAN, Wi-Fi) operates reliably and securely throughout the school;
Manage and maintain the Analog and VoIP telephone systems, as well as the school's servers, data storage, backup, and recovery systems;
Ensure hardware devices such as servers and network equipment (APs, switches) are installed, maintained, and repaired promptly.
Software System Management:
Install, configure, and manage the necessary software systems for educational and administrative operations in the school;
Ensure the stability and security of learning management systems (LMS), student information systems (SIS), and other supporting software.
Information Security:
Develop and implement security policies to protect sensitive data of students, teachers, and staff;
Manage firewall systems, antivirus software, online gaming, and other security measures to prevent external attacks.
Technical Support:
Provide technical support to teachers, students, and staff in the school;
Guide and train staff on how to use IT systems and software.
System Maintenance and Upgrades:
Plan and implement projects to upgrade the school's IT infrastructure;
Monitor, test, and ensure that the hardware and software in use are operating effectively, performing regular maintenance, and upgrading as needed.
Data Storage and Backup Management:
Set up and manage data storage systems, ensuring data security and availability;
Implement backup and data recovery plans to ensure continuous system operation and prevent data loss.
Coordination with Vendors:
Work with partners and vendors to maintain and repair equipment and systems as needed;
Manage contracts, prepare repair proposals, and service requests with vendors related to hardware, software, and IT support services.
User Training and Support:
Organize training sessions on information technology for teachers, staff, and students to enhance the effective use of IT systems;
Provide end-user support for using software, IT tools, and troubleshooting related issues.

benefits:
Mức lương hấp dẫn từ 15.000.000 - 20.000.000 VNĐ, được hưởng đầy đủ các chế độ bảo hiểm & phúc lợi theo quy định của Nhà nước;
Làm việc cùng các chuyên gia có nhiều năm kinh nghiệm trong lĩnh vực, được đào tạo và định hướng để phát triển, có cơ hội thăng tiến lên các vị trí cao hơn sau 1-3 năm gắn bó;
Tận hưởng trọn vẹn các ưu đãi về sản phẩm trong hệ sinh thái của Tập đoàn (Nghỉ dưỡng, khách sạn, nông nghiệp hữu cơ,....);
Văn phòng làm việc đẹp và sáng tạo bậc nhất; Môi trường làm việc trẻ trung, năng động với 85% là 9X.

description:
About KiotViet:
KiotViet aims to extend the significant power of technology to every business model in Vietnam
and Southeast Asia through our simple and effective solutions. We are committed to creating
efficient, convenient products for micro, small, and medium-sized businesses. Over the past 13
years, with a current team of over 1500 people at KiotViet, we recognize that our members are
the foundation of KiotViet and a launchpad for achieving a better KiotViet in the future.
KiotViet is dedicated to creating a work environment that fosters shared success and
responsibilities.
Kiotviet is Vietnam’s largest POS provider, with over 200,000 merchants across various
industries. We are expanding into other South-east Asian countries with our POS offerings and
are expanding our product portfolio with new offerings in the fintech space.
What you will do:
- Participate in all phases of software development, including design analysis and testing;
- Read and understand solution documents and design specifications; collaborate with different teams to fully comprehend product requirements;
- Create test documentation and plans including: test plans, test scenarios, and test cases;
- Execute product testing using both manual and automated approaches;
- Support customers, verify and reproduce issues based on customer feedback; retest software after bug fixes;
- Research and stay updated on testing tools and new knowledge to support the work;
- Propose improvements to products or testing processes;
- Experience working in an Agile/Scrum environment.
Main Responsibilities:
- Perform both manual testing and automation testing for web, mobile, and API;
- Design, develop, and maintain automation test frameworks;
- Build comprehensive test cases based on product requirements and user flows;
- Analyze, report, and track bugs in the system;
- Work closely with the development team to improve product quality;
- Continuously improve testing processes and automation;
- Proactively research and apply new technologies and testing tools;
- Explore and propose ways to apply AI to improve testing efficiency.

benefits:
